Key Design Decisions

valid is qualified with Timer address bit — fires only on Timer accesses
Writing EN=1 to CTRL simultaneously loads VALUE from LOAD register
TIMEOUT sets when VALUE==1 (one cycle before hitting 0)
Write-1-to-clear on STATUS bit 0
Prescaler counter resets when disabled or timer is stopped
Single always block used to avoid driver conflicts


SoC Integration — 3 Changes to riscv.v
Change 1 — Address Constant
veriloglocalparam IO_TIMER_bit = 4;   // after existing IO constants
Change 2 — Module Instance
verilogwire [31:0] timer_rdata;
timer_ip TIMER(
   .clk(clk),
   .rst(!resetn),
   .valid(isIO & mem_wordaddr[IO_TIMER_bit]),
   .we(mem_wstrb),
   .offset(mem_addr[3:2]),
   .wdata(mem_wdata),
   .rdata(timer_rdata)
);
Change 3 — Readback Mux
verilogwire [31:0] IO_rdata =
    mem_wordaddr[IO_UART_CNTL_bit] ? {22'b0, !uart_ready, 9'b0} :
    mem_wordaddr[IO_GPIO_bit]      ? gpio_rdata                  :
    mem_wordaddr[IO_TIMER_bit]     ? timer_rdata                 :
                                     32'b0;

